Changelog: 22-10-2026 23:28:29

Release 0.1.0.

Changelog: 22-10-2026 23:00:01

Added. First version. USB IPS3.5 shows the board's live values on a Turzx USB IPS screen (USB ID 1a86:5722: the Turing
Smart Screen 3.5" and the UsbMonitor 3.5", 5" and 7"), which Linux sees as a USB serial port (cdc_acm), so it needs no
driver. The values are tiles (CPU, GPU, CPU and GPU temperature, VRAM, RAM, fan, VRM and NVMe temperature, network for
all interfaces or a chosen one, each named with its kind: Ethernet, Wi-Fi or virtual, disk, and the weather with an icon
for the sky, a moon at night; choose which) under a header with the user's own text and the time (24 or 12 hours with
AM/PM, the time zone's name or offset from UTC and the date if wanted; summer and winter time follow the system's zone),
in six themes with the user's own text, tile, accent and background colors if wanted (a theme or color being tried
shows in the window's preview only, until it is chosen), on a picture of the user's own if wanted, drawn at the screen's
size in four orientations and updated every second; only the parts that changed are sent, because a whole 3.5" picture
takes almost two seconds over the screen's link. The window shows a preview at the screen's own size (1:1; the 5" and 7"
scaled down) and the screen's state, and sets the brightness, the orientation, the values and Start with the desktop
(minimized). Every command goes to the screen in a USB transfer of its own: the screen drops whatever shares a USB
packet with a command (found on the owner's Turing 3.5": with the pixels in the same write, a picture lost its first 29
pixels and every update after it landed wrong). The screen is reset each time the app connects, so a picture cut off
halfway before (an app that was killed, a cable pulled) cannot shift what follows, and it is found again when it is
plugged back in. The weather comes from Open-Meteo (no account or key) for a place the user searches for, every 30
minutes while its tile is shown; it is the app's only use of the network, and without a place nothing is sent. The
settings are on six tabs (Screen, Values, Look, Clock, Weather, Start). Save picture saves what the screen shows as a
PNG at its own size, Save report every value at that moment, with the date, time and zone, as a text file. Allow access
gives the logged-in user the screen's port with a udev rule (pkexec, once); the screen goes dark when the app quits,
unless that is switched off. Reads the sensors through bc250_core.sensors, without root. The protocol, the reset and the
separate transfers were measured on the owner's board with a Turing Smart Screen 3.5" (22-10-2026).
